{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for complete design-only Source85ee57788e8c6c63c111fa2b6aac9ad2063f8fdf / tree46314fbf504a47d72204cbb0e9644662ada0556e. Primary note read FIRST and FULL (309 lines), then the complete generator, CSS, preview helper and both browser harnesses. Byte-identical reading carries to rebound primaryeb84b45c andarea107195bb. This is the full bc635338 design review under a955/5eee/f89, not a review of only one delta. Three findings remain.\n\nF1 (P2), build.py185–186 and examples/manifest.json: intended update ranges are reported as entryPositionsRead regardless of coverage. In updates-incomplete, entry9 of Change9 is explicitly unavailable and marking is disabled, yet context says that scope was read after8 through9, exactly like the complete state. Summary carousel-updates also uses the full ranges without presenting the entries. The model-context contract must distinguish a known/requested cutoff from entries actually read/presented. Keep missing coverage explicit; do not advertise unread Change9 as read. Check complete, partial and summary contexts against their actual contents. This finding does not allege that the disabled static Mark reviewed writes or advances a shared review point.\n\nF2 (P2), build.py83 and work-offered-storage-{light,dark}.html: Storage agent's offer252 links 'Read the later acceptance' to work-accepted, which displays Interface agent, acceptance253 and subject commitment-interface. This substitutes another offeree's record for storage's own acceptance. Supply the correctly identified storage acceptance and its offer, or label the link as a separate related interface record and keep storage acceptance explicitly unavailable; preserve correct return context. Exercise both agents' offer/acceptance paths rather than only link existence.\n\nF3 (P2), examples/cards.css81 and verification/browser.mjs28: the stated44px target policy is checked only in height. The retained report itself measures36 of648 targets below44px width: standalone File is23.71875px and Diff24.53125px, though both are44px tall. Ten themed page files are affected across all three widths. Add the minimum width/hit area for these controls and check both dimensions for every visible target. Correct the browser evidence and note's blanket claim; the current report's empty small array is a height-only pass, not a44×44 result. The retained render of failed Change23 also shows the narrow standalone Diff.\n\nLifecycle issue resolved before verdict: original primary3c8ca15d/areae146 and request65e22398 are retired, with no approval filed on them. Fresh prepare on this request/promise binds only design childbc635338/promise87dee083 and explicitly closes only that child on a sealed receipt. Full parenta9551a6d and its runtime kit stay open. Do not retire/narrow that parent to declare the kit delivered.\n\nIndependent evidence: all1837 Main95959b92 leaves are exact by path/mode/type/blob;139 new leaves are confined to the note and its directory, producing1976 leaves total. No runtime/test/package/lock source changed. All114 HTML parse, local links/fragments resolve, themes have matching content, full states have Back, no forms/inputs/iframes appear, and preview.js is the only example script. Fully read standard-library generator reproduced114HTML and manifest byte-exact in checker scratch (CLOSED0/e2fa50); no checkout changes or browser rerun. The initial scratch dependency extraction used a wrong Git working directory and stopped before generator execution; it is not passing evidence.\n\nThe112state pages cover56states×2themes. All336 unique state/width records are present at592/390/320; all648 target names/counts/normalized paths match the HTML. All14 retained evidence pins match. All114 rendered input hashes match their browser-run values. Independently reversing only the declared delivered-work unknown-position annotation reconstructs both original generator and manifest hashes, so the continuity claim is corroborated. All8 commit identities,3 scope/incarnation fixtures and7 update entries match the landed design. No reported overflow/broken link/console error is contradicted by this static audit; F3 remains a missing width assertion.\n\nPersonally viewed all14 retained PNGs:5 historical concepts (direction only) and9 current renders, including carousel, question, receipt, failed change, diff, complete updates,320px focus/long-title stress and200% interdiff. Read the complete current source/fixture flow, including separate question approval/decision/conditions/offers, failed/unknown checks, old/unauthorized cards, exact file/diff/interdiff endpoints, complete/incomplete updates, receipt notification retry and clamped refreshed parents. The retained4 browser flow groups and focused contrast/long-text/retry report are builder-attributed local evidence; they do not establish a host, service, real act or complete accessibility audit. Sampled text contrast is at least5.659:1. Only9 current render images are retained, so this does not claim individual visual inspection of336 render combinations.\n\nArchitecture: changes requested for F1/F2/F3. The generic composition, summary/fullscreen distinction, \u003c=2acts, composer free text, exact-revision context, explicit chat handoff and in-place receipt direction follow the amended design. Checked relevant stable MCP Apps host-style variables and context-update semantics (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps/blob/main/specification/2026-01-26/apps.mdx). Runtime app-only detail privacy, exact-revision model act, stale/duplicate-write refusal, host transitions, refresh/focus, bidirectional resize, text fallback and prototype receipt-loop comparison remain S2 test-host witnesses. Static page changes are not host transitions.\n\nSecurity: no additional finding in the bounded static design beyond accurate F1 context. Local helpers perform no signing, live write or service call. Actual per-application sandbox origin, resource-metadata CSP/permissions enforcement, host-held keys/confirmation and app-only tool visibility remain implementation obligations, not claims proved by these files. Unknown publication preserves its original request; receipt-notification retry keeps approval246 rather than repeating approval. Historical concept chat loops do not override current f89 HTML/specification.\n\nSimplification: suitable standard-library static approach, with shared generator/styles and no framework/package/deployment addition. Fixes should stay in those shared paths; no new runtime subsystem is required for these findings. Required planner design read follows a repaired exact-head checker approval. Document-only handling in docs/testing.md avoids a repeated whole gate; no runtime pass is inherited. Capacity's original final gate remains FAILED with its focused repairs and incomplete-case routing separately open; this design verdict neither waives it nor completes capacity, S2 or parenta955.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eb84b45ce42e7147d2c23614bbd13d24083e9cd2","binding":"assigned","head":"85ee57788e8c6c63c111fa2b6aac9ad2063f8fdf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dd7b7167072ea234fc22547f0333841422da5395\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:87dee08305a4e4ad3fc0c8f9d9debfaed4d0356b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:99ea3b4d41217031a70a82f6c84e39b6c8d43a38","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}